Key Dates
List relevant dates such as due dates, lodgment dates, payment dates, and the period the circumstances occurred.

Lodgement / Payment Behaviour
Outline whether obligations were met on time, late, partially paid, or show a pattern of non-compliance.

ATO Engagement
Note any contact with the ATO, including deferral requests, payment plans, or timing of engagement (before or after due date).

Circumstances
Summarise the reasons provided and assess whether they explain the delay or non-compliance.

Impact on Ability (Key Test)
Explicitly determine whether the circumstances prevented lodgment (FTL) or genuinely impacted the ability to pay (GIC).

Mitigation Actions
Identify steps taken to reduce the impact (e.g. follow-ups, prompt lodgment/payment once aware, seeking assistance).

Compliance
Highlight prior lodgment or payment history and whether the behaviour is a one-off issue or part of an ongoing pattern.

Other
Include any additional relevant factors not covered above (e.g. vulnerability, low-risk factors, debt status, agent involvement, or special considerations).

Decision
State whether remission is approved or refused (full or partial) and briefly why.

Action Taken
Record what was done following the decision (e.g. letter issued, penalties remain payable, remission processed).
